# The ledger of `printing`: what a program can do with the system's printers,
# one block per capability, and what Rebel answers. None of Go's, Rust's or
# Python's standard libraries prints (Python's `os.startfile(path, "print")`
# is Windows' shell verb, which this package refuses), so the yardsticks are
# the ones the author named on 2026-11-22: Java's `javax.print`, read on this
# machine that day by `javap -public` of OpenJDK 27's `PrintServiceLookup`,
# `PrintService`, `DocPrintJob`, `CancelablePrintJob`, `DocFlavor`,
# `PrintJobListener` and the standard attributes; Qt Print Support 6.12.0,
# read the same day from `qprinter.h` and `qprinterinfo.h` under Homebrew's
# `qtbase`; and .NET's `System.Drawing.Printing` and `System.Printing` and
# wxWidgets 3.2's printing classes, named from Microsoft's and wxWidgets'
# references and unread on this machine, where neither is installed. Their
# lines are `java`, `qt`, `dotnet` and `wx`.

capability printing/printers  the printers this machine knows, listed with their state
  heroes  printing.printers, printing.Printer, printing.State
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -
  java    PrintServiceLookup.lookupPrintServices, PrintService.getName, PrinterState, PrinterStateReasons, PrinterInfo, PrinterLocation, PrinterMakeAndModel, PrinterIsAcceptingJobs
  qt      QPrinterInfo.availablePrinters, QPrinterInfo.availablePrinterNames, QPrinterInfo.printerName, QPrinterInfo.description, QPrinterInfo.location, QPrinterInfo.makeAndModel, QPrinterInfo.state, QPrinterInfo.isRemote
  dotnet  PrinterSettings.InstalledPrinters, PrintServer.GetPrintQueues, PrintQueue.QueueStatus, PrintQueue.IsOffline, PrintQueue.IsPaused
  wx      -
  note    A printer is a CUPS queue on macOS and Linux and a spooler's printer on Windows, its state in IPP's three words and its reasons in IPP's keywords on both, the spooler's status bits written as those keywords (`media-empty`, `offline-report`, `paused`). An instance of a CUPS queue (its options saved under another name) is no printer and is left out, as Qt and Java leave it out. wxWidgets lists no printers: its dialog chooses one

capability printing/default-printer  the machine's default printer
  heroes  printing.default_printer
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -
  java    PrintServiceLookup.lookupDefaultPrintService
  qt      QPrinterInfo.defaultPrinter, QPrinterInfo.defaultPrinterName, QPrinterInfo.isDefault
  dotnet  PrinterSettings.IsDefaultPrinter, LocalPrintServer.DefaultPrintQueue
  wx      -
  note    none fails `not_found`, where Java answers null and Qt a null printer; a CUPS instance marked the default makes its queue the default

capability printing/printer-named  a printer found by its name
  heroes  printing.printer_named
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -
  java    -
  qt      QPrinterInfo.printerInfo, QPrinterInfo.isNull
  dotnet  PrinterSettings.PrinterName, PrinterSettings.IsValid
  wx      wxPrintData.SetPrinterName
  note    an unknown name fails `not_found`, where Qt answers a null printer and .NET an invalid setting

capability printing/papers  the papers a printer takes, their sizes and unprinted margins
  heroes  printing.papers, printing.Paper
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -
  java    PrintService.getSupportedAttributeValues, MediaSizeName, MediaSize, MediaPrintableArea
  qt      QPrinterInfo.supportedPageSizes, QPrinterInfo.supportsCustomPageSizes, QPrinterInfo.minimumPhysicalPageSize, QPrinterInfo.maximumPhysicalPageSize
  dotnet  PrinterSettings.PaperSizes, PaperSize, PageSettings.PrintableArea, PageSettings.HardMarginX, PageSettings.HardMarginY
  wx      wxPrintPaperDatabase, wxPrintPaperType
  note    A paper is named by its PWG 5101.1 name on every system, IPP's own on CUPS; on Windows the driver's papers are named by their size where it is one of PWG's, and `om_dmpaper-<number>_<w>x<h>mm` where it is not, so every name a list holds names one paper. Lengths are in millimetres, read from hundredths of a millimetre (CUPS) or tenths (Windows) exactly; a Windows paper's margins are read from an information context of the printer set to it

capability printing/default-paper  the paper a printer prints on where a job names none
  heroes  printing.default_paper
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -
  java    PrintService.getDefaultAttributeValue
  qt      QPrinterInfo.defaultPageSize
  dotnet  PrinterSettings.DefaultPageSettings, PageSettings.PaperSize
  wx      wxPrintData.GetPaperId
  note    a printer naming no default fails `not_found`

capability printing/capabilities  whether a printer prints on both sides and in colour, and how many copies it makes
  heroes  printing.capabilities, printing.Capabilities
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -
  java    PrintService.isAttributeValueSupported, PrintService.getSupportedAttributeCategories, Sides, Chromaticity, Copies
  qt      QPrinterInfo.supportedDuplexModes, QPrinterInfo.defaultDuplexMode, QPrinterInfo.supportedColorModes, QPrinterInfo.defaultColorMode, QPrinter.supportsMultipleCopies
  dotnet  PrinterSettings.CanDuplex, PrinterSettings.SupportsColor, PrinterSettings.MaximumCopies
  wx      -
  note    CUPS is asked by `cupsCheckDestSupported` and the `copies-supported` range, Windows by `DeviceCapabilitiesW`; `submit` holds a job to the same answers, failing `unsupported` where Qt would print one side silently

capability printing/settings  what a job asks: copies, paper, orientation, sides, colour, pages and collation
  heroes  printing.Settings, printing.default_settings, printing.Orientation, printing.Sides, printing.ColorMode, printing.PageRange
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -
  java    HashPrintRequestAttributeSet, Copies, MediaSizeName, OrientationRequested, Sides, Chromaticity, PageRanges, SheetCollate
  qt      QPrinter.setCopyCount, QPrinter.copyCount, QPrinter.setPageSize, QPrinter.setPageOrientation, QPrinter.setDuplex, QPrinter.duplex, QPrinter.setColorMode, QPrinter.colorMode, QPrinter.setPageRanges, QPrinter.setFromTo, QPrinter.fromPage, QPrinter.toPage, QPrinter.setPrintRange, QPrinter.printRange, QPrinter.setCollateCopies, QPrinter.collateCopies, QPrinter.setPrinterName, QPrinter.printerName
  dotnet  PrinterSettings.Copies, PrinterSettings.Collate, PrinterSettings.Duplex, PrinterSettings.FromPage, PrinterSettings.ToPage, PrinterSettings.PrintRange, PageSettings.Landscape, PageSettings.Color, PageSettings.PaperSize
  wx      wxPrintData.SetNoCopies, wxPrintData.SetCollate, wxPrintData.SetOrientation, wxPrintData.SetDuplex, wxPrintData.SetColour, wxPrintData.SetPaperId, wxPrintDialogData.SetFromPage, wxPrintDialogData.SetToPage
  note    one record, which `ui`'s print dialog answers and `submit` takes, as Qt's `QPrinter` is both; the four orientations are IPP's, a reverse one printed half a turn on Windows, whose settings have two; page ranges in order and not touching, as IPP's `page-ranges` holds them

capability printing/submit  a PDF document submitted to a printer as one job
  heroes  printing.submit, printing.Job
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -
  java    PrintService.createPrintJob, DocPrintJob.print, SimpleDoc, DocFlavor.INPUT_STREAM.PDF, JobName
  qt      -
  dotnet  -
  wx      -
  note    PDF is the one document form, which CUPS takes on macOS and Linux and Windows' own PDF renderer (`Windows.Data.Pdf`) draws through Direct2D's print control into an XPS job with a print ticket of the settings; never a shell verb. Java takes PDF only where the print service does (no service of Java's own renders one). Qt, .NET and wxWidgets print what a program paints on a page through a painter (`QPainter`, `PrintDocument.PrintPage`, `wxPrintout.OnPrintPage`), which is here `pdf`'s work, the document arriving whole. A page larger than the paper is fitted to it, centred, as CUPS's `print-scaling` of `auto` does

capability printing/status  a job's state, its reasons and the pages printed, told while it runs and when it ends
  heroes  printing.status_of, printing.Status, printing.JobState, printing.is_ended
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -
  java    DocPrintJob.addPrintJobListener, PrintJobListener, PrintJobEvent, JobState, JobStateReasons, JobImpressionsCompleted
  qt      -
  dotnet  PrintSystemJobInfo.JobStatus, PrintSystemJobInfo.NumberOfPagesPrinted, PrintSystemJobInfo.IsCompleted, PrintSystemJobInfo.IsDeleted, PrintSystemJobInfo.Refresh
  wx      -
  note    IPP's seven job states on every system: CUPS's Get-Job-Attributes, the spooler's `GetJobW` on Windows. The spooler forgets a job once it ends, so the layer keeps what this process saw of the jobs it submitted and tells their end then; a job of another process gone from Windows' queue fails `not_found`. Asked, not pushed, as .NET asks it: Java's listener is a callback, which the language takes on no thread of its own

capability printing/jobs  the jobs on a printer that have not ended
  heroes  printing.jobs
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -
  java    -
  qt      -
  dotnet  PrintQueue.GetPrintJobInfoCollection, PrintQueue.NumberOfJobs
  wx      -
  note    oldest first, every user's the system shows

capability printing/cancel  a job cancelled
  heroes  printing.cancel
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -
  java    CancelablePrintJob.cancel
  qt      QPrinter.abort
  dotnet  PrintSystemJobInfo.Cancel
  wx      -
  note    a job that had already ended is no failure, where Java throws `PrintException`; on Windows `JOB_CONTROL_DELETE`, Microsoft's word for a cancel

capability printing/wait  the end of a job waited for, bounded by a span
  heroes  printing.wait, printing.FOREVER
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -
  java    PrintJobListener.printJobNoMoreEvents
  qt      -
  dotnet  -
  wx      -
  note    asked four times a second; fails `timeout` at the span's end and `stopped` once the program's stop is asked (README § A4), in milliseconds, the package standing below `time`

capability printing/raw  a document in the printer's own language sent as it is
  heroes  pending
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -
  java    DocFlavor.BYTE_ARRAY.AUTOSENSE, DocFlavor.INPUT_STREAM.POSTSCRIPT, DocFlavor.INPUT_STREAM.PCL
  qt      -
  dotnet  -
  wx      -
  note    a label printer's ZPL or a PCL stream: CUPS's `application/vnd.cups-raw` and the spooler's `RAW` datatype; it waits for its own block, the spooler's raw path being another arm than the PDF one

capability printing/job-options  the print quality, pages per sheet, scaling, finishing and the input tray asked of a job
  heroes  pending
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -
  java    PrintQuality, NumberUp, Finishings, MediaTray, PrinterResolution
  qt      QPrinter.setResolution, QPrinter.resolution, QPrinterInfo.supportedResolutions, QPrinter.setPaperSource, QPrinter.paperSource, QPrinterInfo.supportedPaperSources, QPrinter.setFullPage, QPrinter.setPageOrder
  dotnet  PrinterSettings.PrinterResolutions, PageSettings.PrinterResolution, PrinterSettings.PaperSources, PageSettings.PaperSource
  wx      wxPrintData.SetQuality, wxPrintData.SetBin
  note    each a setting the printer must be asked whether it takes, as `capabilities` asks sides and colour

capability printing/to-file  a job written to a file instead of a printer
  heroes  refused: the document is a PDF the program already holds, written to a file by `write_file` or `fs`
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -
  java    Destination
  qt      QPrinter.setOutputFileName, QPrinter.outputFileName, QPrinter.setOutputFormat, QPrinter.outputFormat, QPrinter.setPdfVersion, QPrinter.pdfVersion
  dotnet  PrinterSettings.PrintToFile, PrinterSettings.PrintFileName
  wx      wxPrintData.SetFilename
  note    the libraries that paint pages need a file printer to make a PDF; here `pdf` makes it

capability printing/administer  printers added, shared, paused or removed
  heroes  refused: the system's settings do it, with its privileges; a program printing needs none
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -
  java    -
  qt      -
  dotnet  PrintServer.InstallPrintQueue, PrintQueue.Pause, PrintQueue.Resume, PrintQueue.Purge
  wx      -
  note    CUPS's `lpadmin` and Windows' print management ask the administrator's rights

dropped
  java    MultiDocPrintService, MultiDocPrintJob, MultiDoc (several documents in one job: one document a job here); StreamPrintService, StreamPrintServiceFactory (a print service writing to a stream: `pdf` writes the document); ServiceUI (Java's own print dialog: `ui`'s); DocFlavor's other families (one document form, PDF); AttributeSet, HashAttributeSet and the attribute classes' plumbing (one record of settings)
  qt      QPrinter's paint device (newPage, pageRect, paperRect, fullPage, metric, devType, setEngines, QPrintEngine: pages are painted by `pdf`); QPrinter.setPrintProgram, QPrinter.printProgram (a Unix spooler's command: CUPS's library is called); QPrinter.setDocName, QPrinter.docName (the job's title, `submit`'s `title`); QPrinter.setCreator, QPrinter.creator, QPrinter.setFontEmbeddingEnabled, QPrinter.fontEmbeddingEnabled (the document's own, `pdf`'s); QPrinter.setPrinterSelectionOption, QPrinter.printerSelectionOption (raw CUPS options: the settings are one record); QPrinterInfo.isValid (a printer named is found or `not_found`)
  dotnet  PrintDocument, PrintPageEventArgs, PrintController, StandardPrintController, PreviewPrintController (painting pages through events: `pdf` writes the document); PrinterSettings.CreateMeasurementGraphics, PrinterSettings.GetHdevmode, PrinterSettings.SetHdevmode, PrinterSettings.GetHdevnames, PrinterSettings.SetHdevnames (Windows' handles)
  wx      wxPrinter, wxPrintout, wxPrinterDC, wxPrintPreview (painting pages: `pdf`'s); wxPrintDialog, wxPageSetupDialog (`ui`'s dialogs)
